{
  "simulation_id": "sf_homelessness_policy_10actor",
  "title": "San Francisco Homelessness Policy Debate",
  "objective": "Simulate stakeholder negotiations around Proposition C implementation and its impacts on homelessness in San Francisco.",
  "brief": "San Francisco homelessness policy and Proposition C (2018-2022). A business tax to fund $300M in homeless services passed narrowly amid deep community divide. Tent encampments grew despite increased spending. Stakeholders: a small business owner whose storefront foot traffic dropped 60% due to nearby encampments, a street outreach worker with years of trust relationships among unhoused clients who fears forced sweeps will destroy that trust, an ER physician treating 20+ medical emergencies per week from encampments at enormous public cost, and a formerly homeless person now in supportive housing navigating reintegration while mentoring others still on the streets.",
